From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-omap: use optional regulators for capability
 probing

Upstream-Status: Pending [needs review for non-AM335x OMAP SDHCI users]

The OMAP SDHCI capability probe checks pbias and vqmmc regulators to
derive voltage capability bits. Some boards, including AM335x BeagleBone
Black SD-only tiny bring-up, do not model a pbias regulator in DT.

The driver already treats pbias as optional in the real power path via
devm_regulator_get_optional(). Use regulator_get_optional() in the
capability helper too so missing optional supplies do not take the dummy
regulator path and emit misleading boot warnings.

Signed-off-by: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-omap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-omap.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-omap.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-omap.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-omap.c
@@ -945,7 +945,7 @@ static unsigned int sdhci_omap_regulator_get_caps(struct device *dev,
 	struct regulator *reg;
 	unsigned int caps = 0;
 
-	reg = regulator_get(dev, name);
+	reg = regulator_get_optional(dev, name);
 	if (IS_ERR(reg))
 		return ~0U;
 
